It is given that a, b, c and d are four distinct real numbers. Let m_{1}, r_{1} and v_{1} be the mean, the range and the variance of the group of numbers \{a, b, c, d\} respectively while m_{2}, r_{2} and v_{2} be the mean, the range and the variance of the group of numbers \{2a, 2b, 2c, 2d\} respectively. Denote the mean, the range and the variance of the group of numbers \{a+3, b+3, c+3, d+3\} by m_{3}, r_{3} and v_{3} respectively. Which of the following are true?
I. m_{1}+m_{3} > m_{2}
II. r_{1}+r_{3} = r_{2}
III. v_{1}+v_{3} < v_{2}
